# LF in the repo and in every working tree, whatever a clone's core.autocrlf
# says. Several tests hash or byte-compare files on disk, and a CRLF checkout
# fails them with no code change:
#
# - `types/` is emitted by tsc (`npm run types`), which always writes LF, and
#   test/unit/types.test.js byte-compares the checked-in files against a fresh
#   emit.
# - The example knowledge-base records (`examples/*/AIKB/`) are byte-compared
#   against a fresh `kiss-ssg aikb` run, and example 9 and 11 embed their own
#   build script in the page, so the recorded page hash depends on the
#   script's line endings.
# - test/aikb.test.js searches llms.txt for exact line breaks.
#
# `text=auto` leaves binaries alone; nothing here needs CRLF.
* text=auto eol=lf
